        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "In Utah, the average cost to reroof a house ranges from $8,500 to $18,000 for a standard-sized home with basic asphalt shingles. For a typical 2,000-square-foot home, total project costs\u2014including the tear-off of old materials and installation\u2014frequently land near $12,000 to $15,000. Prices shift based on your choice of material, roof pitch, and local labor rates\n\n.",
